{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446147-sect-war-thread-my-cult-s-the-best-cult","id":1446147,"title":"Sect war thread: My cult's the best cult.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-27T13:54:57-07:00","id":1446147,"title":"Sect war thread: My cult's the best cult.","content":"So I felt myself enjoying a good sectarian dispute in another thread and want to see more people involved in this sort of stuff. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Actually the best, really</b><br /> Followers of Set. Great guys and gals, always got your back. Friendliest sect in the game. <br /> <b>Obviously the next Best: </b><br /> Camarilla. A sect for everyone. <br /> <b>Excellent:</b> <br /> Sabbat. Probably the most fun to play, make more sense when you get into it. Not for everyone. <br /> <b>Good</b><br /> Assamites Loyalists- Ninja families looking at court like an all you can eat buffet. <br /> Children of Osiris- I just love saying &quot;OH THE HUMANITY&quot;<br /> Baali Hives. <br /> <b>Ok</b><br /> Inconnu<br /> Ashirra- I'm starting to understand them. There is perhaps a logic to it, but they do seem a bit token on first glance, and they're very underwritten. <br /> Giovanni. It's a family, not a sect, honest. <br /> Not being in a sect.<br /> <b>Bottom tier</b><br /> TBH. They seem like a pretentious lot. <br /> <b>Garbage, doesn't even qualify as a sect. Join if you want to lose the Jyhad</b>. <br /> Anarchs. You're either a poorman's camarilla or a poorman's Sabbat. Fun to play I guess. <br /> <br /> Objectively correct list here. <i>Change my mind </i>(all contesting posts may be reported to the mods for HERESY... oh, there's no rule against that here....)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T14:53:51-07:00","id":1446165,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><b>Sect:</b> A religious body, especially one that has separated from a larger denomination.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>So... Best Sect: </b><br /> The Society of Saint Leopold - <i>&quot;Deus vult, ye spawn of Satan!&quot;</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What? You didn't say it had to be a VAMPIRE sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T15:00:53-07:00","id":1446167,"title":"","content":"I'd put them up with excellent. Perhaps if I were catholic i'd have them the best. As far as hunters go, they're the winners by far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T15:35:40-07:00","id":1446182,"title":"","content":"Anarchs: When you actually think the Brotherhood of Funny Hats is as stupid as it seems.<br /> <br /> Camarilla: WE ARE NOT SILLY!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/QoSLiHKrzRU\" data-code=\"QoSLiHKrzRU\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/QoSLiHKrzRU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Camarilla: Okay, Elysium meetings are a little silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T15:51:51-07:00","id":1446183,"title":"","content":"Best is Giovanni, it's hard to beat the family of family.<br /> Camarilla would be the runner up for having a structure that is relatable to western civilization.<br /> Honorable mention to Followers of Set and Children of Osiris for actually following mythic gods.<br /> Worst would be Anarchs and Sabbat, everyone in the Camarilla knows that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T18:27:27-07:00","id":1446207,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat is the smartest sect - &quot;Hey guys, those crazy ancients are going to wake up and eat all of us. Let's kill them before that happens.&quot; They're all over the place and do lots of dumb things, but in a lot of ways they've got the smartest goal. <br /> <br /> The True Black Hand is the dumbest sect - &quot;Hey guys, when those crazy ancients wake up, let's feed everyone else to them and hope they eat us last.&quot; Yeah, there's no way that plan could go wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T20:53:06-07:00","id":1446215,"title":"","content":"Instead of an already canon Sect, has anyone ever in a Chronicle with a group and/or in a game form their own Sect at all; with the caveat out-of-game prologue to the Chronicle being that the players were moderate-to-high powered low-genned Autarkis who up and decided to join forces to form their own Sect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T21:03:49-07:00","id":1446216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446147-sect-war-thread-my-cult-s-the-best-cult?p=1446207#post1446207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat is the smartest sect - &quot;Hey guys, those crazy ancients are going to wake up and eat all of us. Let's kill them before that happens.&quot; They're all over the place and do lots of dumb things, but in a lot of ways they've got the smartest goal.<br /> <br /> The True Black Hand is the dumbest sect - &quot;Hey guys, when those crazy ancients wake up, let's feed everyone else to them and hope they eat us last.&quot; Yeah, there's no way that plan could go wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, I'd argue the latter is the more rationale explanation.<br /> <br /> To put it into perspective, &quot;Ravnos wakes up and requires three nuclear weapons and a satellite weapon straight from anime to kill. He's also possibly not dead and could kill all his Clan at will.&quot;<br /> <br /> Do you:<br /> <br /> A. Run at him with your Packmates.<br /> <br /> B. Try not to piss him off?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T21:22:42-07:00","id":1446217,"title":"","content":"I mean the answer is to hunt him down and diablarize him before he wakes up. Worked great for getting rid of Tzimisci, Lasombra, Saulot and Cappadocius. (Okay, so it didn't actually work out very well for any of those examples, but I don't believe very many people in-setting actually know about any of that, so the idea that Antediluvians can be killed is pretty widely known).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T21:57:25-07:00","id":1446220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446147-sect-war-thread-my-cult-s-the-best-cult?p=1446215#post1446215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of an already canon Sect, has anyone ever in a Chronicle with a group and/or in a game form their own Sect at all; with the caveat out-of-game prologue to the Chronicle being that the players were moderate-to-high powered low-genned Autarkis who up and decided to join forces to form their own Sect?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's an interesting idea, but I think rather than a handful of Autarkis you might need high up influential members from various independent clans, or even clans in other sects where you could peal off enough members. For a sect to be taken seriously I would think it would need to have at least triple digit members. Unless you meant over a small region like the Oradea League. I love the idea of really high powered games, but player ability really throws things out of whack even from character generation when you say ok spend x amount of experience points on your vampire. The power disparity can be pretty shocking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T22:33:00-07:00","id":1446223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446147-sect-war-thread-my-cult-s-the-best-cult?p=1446215#post1446215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of an already canon Sect, has anyone ever in a Chronicle with a group and/or in a game form their own Sect at all; with the caveat out-of-game prologue to the Chronicle being that the players were moderate-to-high powered low-genned Autarkis who up and decided to join forces to form their own Sect?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> although npcs. in my Philippines game, there are the Aswang Courts of the local eastern kindred which are more like the princedoms of the Dark Ages as they don't have a sect at all, but in certain regions, if a powerful rajah has many vassals, he could form a kingdom/rajahnate under their command. in my game set on an island in the Visayas region, an infernalist Amaranhig (word for Jiang Shi) 6th gen elder with the help of a TMR splinter cult, (reason for the splinter cult is due to the TMR shattering into many secretive cults in my timeline) aided him in conquering rival Aswang domains as he offered them the &quot;join or die&quot; choice which some rajahs agreed into joining him out of fear and became his vassals, but the others are not so lucky. however, there are some eastern kindred that managed to evade him and fled to the domains out of his reach. the infernalist rajah hopes he could attack the Sabbat/Anarchs in the region as they are too busy with their turf wars, but there is a small but stable Cam presence in the region.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25313-raziel","name":"Raziel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T22:54:04-07:00","id":1446224,"title":"","content":"My favorite sect is the Camarilla, that sect is represents the quintessential V:tM game for me. If we go back to 1st and 2nd edition, I liked the Anarchs as well within the context of the Camarilla establishment versus the Anarch struggle. The V5 Anarchs aren\u2019t to my liking, they seem to have become a sort of Sabbat-light. I like the Sabbat as well, and think in many ways a Sabbat game is way easier to play, but I don\u2019t like them as much as the Camarilla. Though I\u2019ve had my own house rules and home brew setting(s) I have been using for years with alternative versions of the Sabbat and Camarilla. <br /> <br /> As for other sects, I like the Giovanni, though I like them as a bloodline more than a Clan. The Hecate are basically a sect now, though I\u2019m not that fond of them as a sect, it seems like they don\u2019t have enough common ground to be a single political entity. <br /> <br /> The idea of the True Black Hand is kinda cool, but in practice there are many silly aspects to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T23:44:18-07:00","id":1446227,"title":"","content":"...fearing Gehenna seems kinda silly when the antes, while awake, never did anything so apocalyptic. Not entire\u00f6y silly enough to disniss the idea out of hand: maybe they'll revive in Wassail... But when Capa and lasombra roamed the earth they didnt do much. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446147-sect-war-thread-my-cult-s-the-best-cult?p=1446215#post1446215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of an already canon Sect, has anyone ever in a Chronicle with a group and/or in a game form their own Sect at all; with the caveat out-of-game prologue to the Chronicle being that the players were moderate-to-high powered low-genned Autarkis who up and decided to join forces to form their own Sect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Small cults/tiny sects are very common. I use them often. IMO, &quot;Anarch&quot; is a blanket derogatory term that could mean something as benign as 'The prince's moderate opposition&quot; all the way to &quot;These guys who made their own &quot;sect&quot; with blackjack and hookers.&quot; Autuarks is often used for even more extreme groups that even anarchs don't get along with (but may just be a stuborn old-system domain. Autuark means &quot;independent&quot; really) and anethema is used for kill-on-sight types. <br /> Maybe once a sect reaches a sufficient size and age it'll be taken seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T00:06:26-07:00","id":1446229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446147-sect-war-thread-my-cult-s-the-best-cult?p=1446217#post1446217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the answer is to hunt him down and diablarize him before he wakes up. Worked great for getting rid of Tzimisci, Lasombra, Saulot and Cappadocius. (Okay, so it didn't actually work out very well for any of those examples, but I don't believe very many people in-setting actually know about any of that, so the idea that Antediluvians can be killed is pretty widely known).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. Because the very people that &quot;know&quot; the Antediluvians can be killed are also the same people that believe they exist. For the vast majority of Kindred, the Antediluvians are metaphorical or flat out don't exist. I always liked this element because it's the perfect con job of the Inner Council. As long as they deny the Antediluvians exist, they are the highest authority in the world. All they have to do is outlive the majority of Kindred.<br /> <br /> Yes, MITHRAS knows better but that's part of why he finds the Camarilla ridiculous.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, yes, some random 5th Generation embraced after Rome claims to be the most powerful vampire in the world. Also, a Spanaird. I mean, not even an Iberian.&quot;<br /> <br /> It also adds to the mystique of the Sabbat as they are fighting for a Crusade that will strike most Kindred as insane.<br /> <br /> &quot;Caine? What? Dude, I'm Hindu!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T04:58:35-07:00","id":1446273,"title":"","content":"I lean into the idea that the the Camarilla views itself as the UNIVERSAL government of vampires. You are considered to be under the Camarilla's authority unless you are one of the unfortunate few to actually be on the Shit List. They don't even acknowledge other movements as EXISTING, generally---a Neonate embraced in a Camarilla city in the Western World probably won't know what the Sabbat is beyond vague stories of &quot;murderous vampires in the wilds.&quot; They'll only know about the Anarchs if they talk to Anarchs. Powerful Methuselahs who can scoff at the Camarilla's claim of authority like Mithras of London, Siegfried of Vancouver, and Marcus Vitel in Washington D.C. are limited to rumour outside their sphere of influence. For young Kindred in an American city these are wild tales, while the Authority of the local Prince seems paramount and absolute. Of course this culture of silence actually feeds into the mystique and lends credence when an Anarch Legate or Sabbat recruiter appears at the Rants or in the Racks of a Camarilla Domain. The Streisand Effect does some of the work for radical Sects in bringing curious young childer to their door. But since the Camarilla doesn't even recognize these other positions generally, a vampire might find themselves summoned to court or even appointed to a role in the Domain regardless of whatever allegience they profess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T09:18:50-07:00","id":1446294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446147-sect-war-thread-my-cult-s-the-best-cult?p=1446215#post1446215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of an already canon Sect, has anyone ever in a Chronicle with a group and/or in a game form their own Sect at all; with the caveat out-of-game prologue to the Chronicle being that the players were moderate-to-high powered low-genned Autarkis who up and decided to join forces to form their own Sect?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thinking on this I'm starting to picture it, do you have any ideas how it will be implemented by the players? Are they taking over a series of cities as princes or growing from a secret society? Do they have Childer as members/enforcers? Curious since I often wonder what people think it will take to do things on a large scale. Always running games, a lot of the behind the scenes stuff going on I imagine would be picked apart to one degree or another by players if they were reading it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T09:33:33-07:00","id":1446296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446147-sect-war-thread-my-cult-s-the-best-cult?p=1446224#post1446224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for other sects, I like the Giovanni, though I like them as a bloodline more than a Clan. The Hecate are basically a sect now, though I\u2019m not that fond of them as a sect, it seems like they don\u2019t have enough common ground to be a single political entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Giovanni make a perfect Ventrue Bloodline, dropping the whole Necomancy bit for Auspex Dominate Fortitude for the &quot;I see dead people&quot; following the Sabbat Ventrue, and Dominate Fortitude Potence for the family enforcer types. This may just be my dislike of Blood Magic shining through again though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T10:22:51-07:00","id":1446303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446147-sect-war-thread-my-cult-s-the-best-cult?p=1446294#post1446294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thinking on this I'm starting to picture it, do you have any ideas how it will be implemented by the players? Are they taking over a series of cities as princes or growing from a secret society? Do they have Childer as members/enforcers? Curious since I often wonder what people think it will take to do things on a large scale. Always running games, a lot of the behind the scenes stuff going on I imagine would be picked apart to one degree or another by players if they were reading it.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the most part, it'd be a landless Sect entirely; with maybe one central headquarters, sort of like how the TBH or Inconnu would do it. Trying to do the style of gaining actual hard-influence control of different cities would just get the players hunted out by the Camarilla. So secret society as you suggest. <br /> <br /> Large scale stuff has always been easy to do and behind-the-scene/downtime certain stuff, with merely an Influence background roll then narrative the things moving in motion on the degree of success the roll garnered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}